<resources>
    <!--
      The Compose UI already follows the system via isSystemInDarkTheme(), but the *window* behind
      it comes from this theme. With only a Light theme declared, a phone in dark mode showed a
      white window for the moment between launch and Compose's first frame — a white flash on every
      cold start, which reads as a bug.

      The platform has no Theme.Material.DayNight (that parent is AppCompat's), so the light/dark
      split is done the resource-qualifier way instead: this file is the light theme, and
      values-night/themes.xml declares the dark one under the same name.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Commute" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar">
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@color/window_background</item>
    </style>
</resources>
